# GitHub Linguist overrides — keep the repository "Languages" bar reflecting the
# Python framework. Linguist ranks languages by committed byte count, so the
# single ~0.5 MB standalone HTML share under design/ was being counted as ~70%
# of the repo even though the actual code (domains + bundle) is Python.
#
# The design/ package is customer-facing DOCUMENTATION (draw.io diagram sources,
# their PNG exports, OVERVIEW.md, and the generated datalab-customer-overview.html
# share) — not framework source — so it is excluded from language statistics.
# The framework code, tests, jobs, notebooks and scripts (all Python) are
# unaffected and continue to drive the bar.
#
# Reference: https://github.com/github-linguist/linguist/blob/main/docs/overrides.md
# (GitHub recomputes the bar on push; it can take a few minutes / a cache cycle.)

design/**                               linguist-documentation

# The standalone share is GENERATED (regenerated out-of-band, see AGENTS.md /
# the maintain-design-diagram skill) — also collapse it in diffs.
design/datalab-customer-overview.html   linguist-generated
# The pipeline inventory is rendered from config/ by `make design`.
design/PIPELINES.md                     linguist-generated
